WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:03.100
We've been waiting for weeks and it is happening.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:08.690
The house today is expected to vote to send
articles of Donald Trump's impeachment to

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.690
the Senate.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.830
This is the first step in starting that Senate
impeachment trial of Donald Trump, which in

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:19.320
all likelihood is going to lead to Donald
Trump's acquittal by the Republican controlled

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.320
Senate.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.659
At which point the question will be, does
that acquittal bolster Donald Trump's chances

00:00:24.659 --> 00:00:29.569
of winning in November or does it hurt Donald
Trump's chances of winning the house also

00:00:29.569 --> 00:00:34.000
is expected to name impeachment managers who
will prosecute the case.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.950
We may already know who those managers are.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.400
By the time you watch this clip or listen
to today's show, that decision may have already

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.620
been made according to NPR.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.500
Following today's vote, the house will inform
the Senate.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.950
It is ready to transmit the articles across
the Capitol.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:53.040
The Senate will respond that it is ready to
receive them and a formal procession and reception

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.560
will take place.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.210
That could happen later today.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:00.700
The trial again based on what we know right
now expected to start in less than a week

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:07.510
on Tuesday, January 21st that means we will
in all likelihood have to reschedule the David

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.790
Pakman show viewer tournament.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.350
Heartbreaking to many in our audience.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:15.200
I know I will have more information about
that by the end of the week.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.090
Republicans are of course already trying to
limit the witnesses that will appear.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:23.790
Republicans are talking about uh, having some
portions of the trial completely behind closed

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.090
doors clearing the Senate chamber.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:32.010
So that debate is going to get very interesting
very quickly and there are also a ton of new

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:37.540
documents that should be part of the impeachment
trial that are explosive, which I will talk

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.360
to you about a little bit later.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.150
This is only the third time in history that
there will be an impeachment trial.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.560
Andrew Johnson, bill Clinton being the other
two.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.619
Remember that there was no impeachment trial
against Richard Nixon.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:56.640
Nixon resigned before being impeached after
he knew he had lost the support of the Republican

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.240
voters and of Republicans in the Senate.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:04.150
He would have been impeached and convicted
and chose to resign to avoid that.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:08.690
The difference, one of the differences between
Nixon in the 70s and Trump in 2020 is Trump

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.860
has Fox news, Trump has social media.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.420
Trump has one of the most low information,
electorates to put it lightly that we've seen

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.480
in a long time.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.900
So Trump has and likely will not lose the
support of his sycophantic base, nor of the

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.170
Republican Senate.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:30.940
A very different scenario today than what
we had under Richard Nixon.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:34.940
So just a short update, this is happening
more than likely tomorrow.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.330
Once we know who will be managing impeachment,
the parameters of it, the expected duration

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.010
of the trial, tomorrow we'll have more of
a plan for how we'll be covering it, what

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.390
to expect.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.230
Maybe we will start to get a sense of which
witnesses will or won't be included, what

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.220
documents will or won't be included.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.640
Uh, and that is exactly what we have to talk
about next.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:04:48.590
The new documents that we are now

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:53.900
aware of.

